[38;2;124;124;124mActually, I realize I should double-check: is the pullback under doubling map a [0m[38;2;124;124;124m*von Neumann subalgebra* (weakly closed)? The pullback φ*L^\infty = {f∘φ} is the[0m[38;2;124;124;124mset of functions measurable w.r.t. the σ-algebra φ^{-1}(Borel). This is a sub-σ-[0m[38;2;124;124;124malgebra. L^\infty of a sub-σ-algebra is a von Neumann subalgebra of L^\infty of [0m[38;2;124;124;124mthe full σ-algebra. Yes, this is standard: sub-σ-algebras ↔ von Neumann [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msubalgebras of L^\infty. ✓.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAnd it's proper because the sub-σ-algebra φ^{-1}(B) ⊊ Borel[0,1] (e.g., [0,1/2] [0m[38;2;124;124;124mis not in φ^{-1}(B) for any B... well [0,1/2] is Borel; is it φ^{-1}(B) for some[0m[38;2;124;124;124mB? φ^{-1}([0,1/2]) = [0,1/4]∪[1/2,3/4] ≠ [0,1/2]. And more generally the σ-[0m
[38;2;124;124;124malgebra φ^{-1}(B) consists of sets symmetric under t↦t+1/2 mod 1, which [0,1/2] [0m[38;2;124;124;124mis not). ✓.[0m

